  "details": "If we have access to the instance type in the avatar parameters, we could control which features can be used on an avatar.\nBeing able to disable some avatar features in public worlds, would be a really good way to prevent people to abuse some of those features to annoy people.\nI like to mess around with unity a lot, but I'm always skeptical to make my avatars public because people would probably use those features to harass others...\nBut if I make them only usable in a friends+ or higher wouldn't be such an issue in my opinion, as the players in the world have more control over who is allowed to be in there.",
